{{also|de-toxify}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[de-toxify]]

===Etymology===
Attested since 1905 (twelve years earlier than ''[[toxify]]''), from {{affix|en|de-|tox|alt2=tox-|-ify}}. ({{m|en|detoxicate|Detoxicate}} is attested one year earlier, since 1904.)

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[remove]] [[foreign]] and [[harmful]] [[substance]]s from something.
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Transactions of the American Pediatric Society|volume=18|page=295|year=1907|passage=As a result of this, in some way or other, unknown to us, a diminished power of oxidation results and the organism loses the power to '''detoxify''' substances absorbed from the intestine which have been present there in excess; these circulate in the blood, exerting their poisonous action and cannot be excreted by the kidneys because they are not brought to them in the proper form.|title=Some possible etiological factors in the recurrent vomiting of children|author=John Howland}}

